<TD colSpan=2><SPAN class=abs><B><FONT size=2>THE raunchy television commercial promoting Gap jeans featured rock icon Madonna smiling sexily from beneath a tweed cap. </FONT></B></SPAN>
<P><SPAN class=abs><FONT size=2>A pair of low-slung blue denims clung to her narrow hips, <STRONG>showing off a perfect body. <BR></STRONG><BR>The camera captured exactly the sort of look that thousands of other women immediately wanted to copy. <BR><BR><STRONG>The Madonna jeans campaign was a brilliant marketing success for the High Street store in the autumn of last year.</STRONG> <BR><BR><STRONG>The fun and funky hipsters modelled by the 44-year-old singer flew off the shelves, boosting</STRONG> the already booming multi-million pound jeans market in Britain and America. <BR><BR><STRONG>Yet a few months later, in the spring of this year, a very different image of Gap jeans was revealed to the world.</STRONG></FONT></SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=abs><FONT size=2>click<STRONG> Read More</STRONG> for the full article. <BR><BR></P></FONT></SPAN></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></P>
</font></div>
